    rdfs:label "Evidence for Skins Furs Pelts Goat undressed used in Leather Tanning, Tawing & Currying: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. LEATHER"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "Curaudau has employed with advantage a steep of dilute sulphuric acid. Morocco leather.--The true morocco leather is goat skin tanned and then dyed on the side of the grain."@en ;
